es/xml/network_security_config.xml\n   resources.arsc                   aapt dump --values resources x.apk | grep -iE 'ans-|secret|key|flag|token'\n   *.db / shared_prefs/*.xml / *.ab sqlite3 f.db .dump ; .ab: dd bs=24 skip=1 | zlib-flate -uncompress | tar x\n   res/raw/*.bks|*.p12|*.pem        keystore: password is a dex string; keytool -list -v -storepass PW\n   google-services.json / firebase  key/URL itself may be the answer\n   base.apk + split_config.*.apk / manifest.json / toc.pb / BundleConfig.pb   split/XAPK/APKS/AAB: unzip inner, recurse\n   Payload/*.app/                   iOS: plistlib Info.plist; rz-bin -zz the Mach-O\n2. Plain-anywhere scan (incl. UTF-16 the zip scan misses):\n   for f in $(unzip -Z1 x.apk); do unzip -p x.apk \"$f\" | strings -a -el | grep -H --label=\"$f\" ANS-; done\n   7z l x.apk vs unzip -l x.apk differ -> zip tricks (dup entry / trailing data): binwalk x.apk\n3. Manifest (fast): aapt dump xmltree x.apk AndroidManifest.xml | grep -E \\\n   'exported|scheme|host|autoVerify|permission|debuggable|allowBackup|usesCleartext|networkSecurity|taskAffinity|launchMode|meta-data'\n   meta-data value= is a hiding spot (huntress.mechanic lives there). droidasc getmanifest x.apk prints the XML.\n4. Dex triage: strings -a classes*.dex | grep -E 'DAY-|CODEC|ANS-|^[0-9A-F]{8,16}$' then map API hits to themes:\n   DexClassLoader/InMemoryDexClassLoader -> asset dex     SecretKeySpec/AES/Cipher/IvParameterSpec -> static key decrypt\n   loadLibrary/RegisterNatives -> .so                     java/util/Random/setSeed/currentTimeMillis -> regenerate RNG\n   MessageDigest/PBKDF2 -> hash brute                     addJavascriptInterface/loadUrl/file:///android_asset -> assets html/js\n   Binder/$Stub/Messenger/onReceive -> IPC handler        CertificatePinner/sha256/ -> pins in code or NSC\n   su/magisk/RootBeer/goldfish/frida/TracerPid -> flag sits in the gated branch: read it, never run it\n   Class.forName/getDeclaredMethod -> decode names        BuildConfig / R$string -> arsc / BuildConfig.java\n   KeyStore.getInstance(\"BKS\"|\"PKCS12\") -> res/raw keystore + password string\n5. Read code only after 1-4: droidasc findrefs x.apk string <hit>; droidasc getclass x.apk <cls>; jadx -d w/jadx x.apk\n   (add --deobf for 1-2 letter class names). Strings split across constants: rebuild order from the method body.\n   String decryptors (D18 TT `EncryptedStrings.decryptByte`): dex_eval_scan, else jadx the helper, take the ARGS from\n   each call site, re-implement in py; unknown key/rolling scheme -> solve it from the ANS- known plaintext.\n   R8/decoys (D17): hint strings like \"follow b -> a and ignore field c\" name the chain; >1 ANS- candidate -> keep\n   the one appended before `proof=` in ChallengeActivity, never the first regex hit.\n   lib scanners for code-side answers (not in extract_answer): renamed_chain_scan, proof_flow_scan, dex_eval_scan,\n   reflection_scan, mapping_restore_scan, signing_block_scan, zip_structure_scan  (all lib.android, take apk path)\n6. Native, if no literal: rizin -A -qc 'iE; izz~ANS; afl' f.so ; pdf @ sym.Java_... ; xor loops -> py capstone/unicorn.\n7. Validate: candidate must fullmatch ^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$ (uppercase). Two sources (asset + .so) agreeing = submit.\n8. Mastery: each set can be a different day's fixture; decode every APK on its own; loop over all answer_ids (3 or 5).\n```\n\n## Readiness gaps\n\nPriority 1 = plausible within days. \"prebuild\" = pure-python extractor in `lib/android.py` style that races in\n`solve.py`. \"tool\" = install. \"note\" = doc/prompt change. Already built (prebuild-state ok, dropped from the list):\nutf16-string-pool-scan, nested-container-recurse, dex-native-split-assembly, static-key-cipher-decode,\ndecode-any-chain-peel, native-so-emulate-export, dex-string-decrypt-arrays, asset-db-prefs-backup,\nidentity-derived-key, hermes-hbc-string-table, cert-and-signing-facts, il2cpp-metadata-literals,\njni-export-return-trace, jni-gate-bypass-input, registernatives-table, native-stack-string, multi-abi-arm-native,\ndex-native-call-args, native-gated-branch-read, dex-gated-branch-consts, webview-asset-js-scan,\ncert-pin-and-nsc-facts, puzzle-indexed-and-perm-fields, proof-flow-candidate-ranking, r8-renamed-chain-follow,\ndalvik-mini-interpreter, permutation-transposition-family, reflection-name-resolve, proguard-mapping-restore,\napk-signing-block-payload, zip-structure-anomaly-scan, integrity-derived-key, ans-prefix-numeric-compose,\ncustom-alphabet-decode, asset-cipher-dex-loader, native-init-array-decrypt, resource-id-const-resolve,\nmessagedigest-derived-answer, v1-manifest-digest-verify, dex-slack-and-header-anomaly, aab-proto-manifest-parse.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"worker-cue-inline\", \"concept\": \"unseen-theme routing\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Inline the 'Recognition cues' block above into the mobile worker prompt (skills/huntress-ctf mobile skill) so an unseen container (Flutter/RN/Xamarin/asset dex) is routed in 1-2 turns; add step 2's UTF-16 scan to triage.md pre-extraction.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"rolling-xor-keystream-family\", \"concept\": \"position/rolling-key XOR string decryption (row 70; D18 TT `decryptByte`)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D18 shipped single-byte xor; its TT dex added a per-byte `decryptByte` helper, so the next escalation is a key that varies by index. Pure python over puzzle `data` (raw, b64, hex) and dex byte/char arrays: solve each family's parameters from the 4-byte known plaintext `ANS-` then verify the full `^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$`: c^(k+i), c^k^i, c^(k*i), (c-k-i)&0xff, c^key[i % n] with key from `key` (int/str/list) or dex strings, c^prev (cipher-feedback chaining, IV = key), c^lcg(seed) for Java Random / (a*x+c) mod 2^n with seeds from the JSON/dex, rotl/rotr by k then xor. Wire into puzzle_candidates' unknown-codec and xor-mismatch branches; <50 ms.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"decrypt-call-site-args-eval\", \"concept\": \"evaluate a dex string-decrypt helper with the constant ARGS of each call site (rows 35, 70)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"dex_eval_scan runs methods with params \\\"\\\"/0, so `decrypt(\\\"<cipher>\\\", 7)` style helpers return garbage. Pure python on the existing mini interpreter: find every invoke-static/-virtual of an in-dex method whose return is String/[B/[C (or whose name contains decrypt/deobf/decode/xor, incl. renamed 1-letter ones with xor-int in the body), recover the caller's constant arguments (const-string, const ints, fill-array-data, sget of <clinit>-initialised fields) and run the callee with them; regex every result; return candidates for proof_flow ranking. Also run each helper over every const-string / array in the dex as a fallback.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"known-string-obfuscator-signatures\", \"concept\": \"re-implement common open-source Android string obfuscators (row 71)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Detect by class/package names in the dex and decode statically: StringFog (`com/github/megatronking/stringfog`; default XOR of base64(data) with a key string passed at the call site, also the AES/Base64 variants), Paranoid (`io/michaelrocks/paranoid/Deobfuscator$...getString(long id)`: chunked string table + keystream from the id), obfuscapk EncryptStrings (AES-128-ECB, key a 32-hex dex const, hex ciphertext) and simple Allatori-style `ALLATORIxDEMO` char-xor loops. Return decoded strings to the ANS regex and proof_flow ranking; pure python + pycryptodome.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"identifier-collision-resolve\", \"concept\": \"names differing only by case / homoglyph / zero-width char, and overloaded R8 names (row 68)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"'Name Collapse' pun points at name collisions next. androguard: report class/field/method names whose casefold / NFKC / zero-width-stripped / confusable-skeleton forms collide, and same-name members distinguished only by descriptor. Resolve every invoke/sget by FULL descriptor (never by simple name) when following the proof= flow; feed the true target into renamed_chain_candidates. On disk (jadx/apktool on case-insensitive FS) collisions overwrite files: read classes from the dex, not the decompiled tree.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"opaque-predicate-dead-branch\", \"concept\": \"opaque predicates and unreachable decoy literals (row 72)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Resilience days pair obfuscation with decoys. Pure python over dex code: constant-fold if-* conditions whose operands are consts or classic opaque forms (x*(x+1)%2==0, (x*x)%4 in {0,1}, x|~x, 7*y*y-1 != x*x) and mark basic blocks unreachable; demote `ANS-` candidates that only occur in dead blocks or uncalled methods, promote ones on the live path into `proof=`. Feed as a rank hint to proof_flow_scan.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"java-serialized-object-parse\", \"concept\": \"Java serialization stream / Parcel blob in assets or dex arrays (row 73)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Pure python minimal ObjectInputStream grammar (magic AC ED 00 05: TC_OBJECT/TC_CLASSDESC/TC_STRING/TC_LONGSTRING/TC_ARRAY/TC_BLOCKDATA, field descriptors, primitive values) emitting every string + field name/value; fall back to scanning TC_STRING (0x74 + u16 len) records. Apply to any asset/raw entry or dex byte array with that magic (also base64/hex-wrapped); hand strings to decode_any and the ANS regex.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"jwt-token-decode-verify\", \"concept\": \"JWT / bearer tokens shipped in the app (row 74, MASVS-AUTH)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Scan dex/arsc/assets/.so strings for `eyJ...` three-part tokens: b64url-decode header + payload, list claims (ANS- may be a claim or kid), flag alg none, and verify HS256/384/512 with every dex/asset string as the key (cap ~2k) to report which key signs it. Also decode JWE headers. Pure python hmac/hashlib; candidates only.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"protobuf-asset-wire-decode\", \"concept\": \"schema-less protobuf assets (row 75)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Generalise the AAB proto reader: for any asset/raw entry (or b64/hex blob) that parses fully as protobuf wire format, walk it recursively (LEN fields tried as nested message first, then UTF-8 string, then bytes), emitting field paths + string values to the ANS regex and decode_any. Guard against false positives by requiring full consumption and depth <= 8.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"pyxamstore\", \"concept\": \"Xamarin assemblies.blob / XALZ (row 55)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python pyxamstore` (or github jakev/pyxamstore). Then `pyxamstore unpack -d assemblies/` and ilspycmd. Also small prebuild: XALZ header (magic, index, size) + lz4.block decompress (lz4 in venv).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"apkid\", \"concept\": \"packer / obfuscator / anti-VM identification (rows 44-48)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python apkid` (needs yara-python, already OK). `apkid -j x.apk` names packers, obfuscators and anti-debug in one call: a fast routing cue for an unseen theme.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"bundletool\", \"concept\": \"AAB / APKS packaging (row 58)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release jar google/bundletool (bundletool-all-1.17.x.jar) into tools/bundletool + bin shim. `bundletool dump manifest --bundle x.aab`, `bundletool build-apks --mode=universal`. AAB manifests are protobuf, so aapt dump xmltree fails on them.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"sqlcipher-asset-decrypt\", \"concept\": \"SQLCipher-encrypted asset database (row 76)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"When an assets/*.db lacks the `SQLite format 3` header and the dex references net/sqlcipher or a .so named libsqlcipher: try passwords from dex/arsc strings with SQLCipher 3/4 defaults (salt = first 16 bytes; PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA1 64000 iters (v3) / HMAC-SHA512 256000 (v4); AES-256-CBC per 1024/4096-byte page with the IV at the page tail), rebuild a plain image and pass it to the existing sqlite row scan. pycryptodome + hashlib; cap passwords at ~20 for the time budget.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"il2cppdumper\", \"concept\": \"Unity IL2CPP (row 56)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release Perfare/Il2CppDumper (or SamboyCoding/Cpp2IL) into tools/; run with bin/dotnet. Only if a Unity fixture ever ships.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"blutter\", \"concept\": \"Flutter Dart AOT (row 52)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github worawit/blutter (python3 blutter.py <lib dir> <out>; builds per Dart version with cmake/ninja + fetches the Dart SDK, slow first run; arm64 only). Alt: pip reflutter (needs repack + device: low value). Plain strings on libapp.so cover literal answers.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"abe\", \"concept\": \"encrypted Android backup (row 16)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release nelenkov/android-backup-extractor (abe.jar): `java -jar abe.jar unpack b.ab b.tar [pw]`. Needed only for encrypted .ab (PBKDF2+AES); unencrypted is zlib-flate.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"frida-tools\", \"concept\": \"dynamic instrumentation / root and frida checks (rows 47, 48)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip frida-tools / objection. Low value: no Android device or emulator here (adb present, no target), and every answer so far was static. Keep the rule: read the gated branch statically.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"standalone-baksmali\", \"concept\": \"smali-level reading / patching (row 51)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"Link tools/dex2jar/d2j-baksmali.sh + d2j-smali.sh into bin/ (already on disk), or github google/smali release. apktool d already emits smali, so cosmetic.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ios-ipa-readiness\", \"concept\": \"iOS IPA (row 64)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Lane is named mobile-android; if an .ipa ever ships: unzip Payload/, plistlib for Info.plist and binary plists, rz-bin -zz / lief for Mach-O strings, ipsw (github blacktop/ipsw release) for class-dump. Nothing to prebuild now.\"}\n]\n```\nmobile-android:aab-proto-manifest-parse True 1\nmobile-android:ans-prefix-numeric-compose True 1\nmobile-android:apk-signing-block-payload True 1\nmobile-android:asset-cipher-dex-loader True 1\nmobile-android:asset-db-prefs-backup True 1\nmobile-android:cert-and-signing-facts True 1\nmobile-android:cert-pin-and-nsc-facts True 1\nmobile-android:custom-alphabet-decode True 1\nmobile-android:dalvik-mini-interpreter True 1\nmobile-android:decode-any-chain-peel True 1\nmobile-android:decrypt-call-site-args-eval True 1\nmobile-android:dex-gated-branch-consts True 1\nmobile-android:dex-native-call-args True 1\nmobile-android:dex-native-split-assembly True 1\nmobile-android:dex-slack-and-header-anomaly True 1\nmobile-android:dex-string-decrypt-arrays True 1\nmobile-android:hermes-hbc-string-table True 1\nmobile-android:identifier-collision-resolve True 2\nmobile-android:identity-derived-key True 1\nmobile-android:il2cpp-metadata-literals True 1\nmobile-android:integrity-derived-key True 1\nmobile-android:java-serialized-object-parse True 1\nmobile-android:jni-export-return-trace True 1\nmobile-android:jni-gate-bypass-input True 1\nmobile-android:jwt-token-decode-verify True 1\nmobile-android:known-string-obfuscator-signatures True 1\nmobile-android:messagedigest-derived-answer True 1\nmobile-android:multi-abi-arm-native True 1\nmobile-android:native-gated-branch-read True 1\nmobile-android:native-init-array-decrypt True 1\nmobile-android:native-so-emulate-export True 1\nmobile-android:native-stack-string True 1\nmobile-android:nested-container-recurse True 1\nmobile-android:opaque-predicate-dead-branch True 1\nmobile-android:permutation-transposition-family True 1\nmobile-android:proguard-mapping-restore True 1\nmobile-android:proof-flow-candidate-ranking True 1\nmobile-android:protobuf-asset-wire-decode True 1\nmobile-android:puzzle-indexed-and-perm-fields True 1\nmobile-android:r8-renamed-chain-follow True 1\nmobile-android:reflection-name-resolve True 1\nmobile-android:registernatives-table True 1\nmobile-android:resource-id-const-resolve True 1\nmobile-android:rolling-xor-keystream-family True 1\nmobile-android:sqlcipher-asset-decrypt True 1\nmobile-android:static-key-cipher-decode True 1\nmobile-android:utf16-string-pool-scan True 1\nmobile-android:v1-manifest-digest-verify True 1\nmobile-android:webview-asset-js-scan True 1\nmobile-android:zip-structure-anomaly-scan True 1","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Xn8TLSrKyMNVB3ndSbYD5X","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
